 activities  start at just 50 of your normal  intensity  start with light walks stationary biking  yoga  pilates or low intensity body weight  strength and conditioning training  keep the duration of your exercise under  15 minutes  here are some exercises on my youtube  channel which you can follow  all the links will be in my description  box below  so this phase is to ease you slowly back  into exercising without putting  too much strain on your body if you do  experience  chest pain headache dizziness shortness  of breath or  rapid breathing then you need to ease  back and take it down a notch by  reducing  your workout time or reduce the  intensity  even more  as you move into phase 2 or week 2  you can start to increase the workout  duration to 15  to 30 minutes you can still continue  with the activities from phase 1  but increase the workout duration and  intensity slightly more  so at this phase you should be able to  hold a full conversation without  difficulty  when performing light intensity  exercises so here are some exercises on  my youtube channel which you can follow  as well  again i've created a playlist and all  the links  will be in my description box below  [Music]  now that you have been active for 2  weeks and slowly regained your stamina  in phase 3 or week 3 you can start to  increase the workout intensity to 75  percent of your pre covered fitness  this is where you can include weight  training and circuit training  so start by performing slightly more  intense exercises with a block of  recovery  and include two to three times of weight  lifting  to build your strength and muscle mass  you can also start to increase your  workout duration  from 30 to 45 minutes  once again you can follow the homework  videos on my youtube channel  right here  as we enter into the final phase which  is week  4 this should challenge your  coordination  strength and also endurance in this  phase  it can be a mixture of body weight  exercises  circuit training and weight lifting if  you are  feeling that you're back to your usual  self you can increase the workout  intensity  even more and workout duration from  45 to 60 minutes i've included  some slightly more intense workouts  which you can check it out right here on  my youtube channel  after the entire four weeks if you feel  that you have fully recovered  then you can resume back to your usual  workout routine however it is still  very important for you to monitor  yourself after  each workout session if there is  abnormal breathlessness  abnormal heart rate excessive fatigue or  chest pain  it is very important for you to stop any  activities or  ease up and seek advice from a  healthcare professional  while exercising is important for your  health and recovery journey  it is also essential to avoid pushing  yourself too far  doing so could slow down your recovery  or  cause your symptoms to worsen by  increasing the levels of  inflammation in the body so listen to  your body  take it slow and follow these four  phases  by gradually reintroducing exercise  into your routine in most countries  fitness centers are still shut  and some countries might not allow  outdoor activities to stop the spread of  kobe 19.  so i hope that my home-based workout  videos will continue to keep you active  and healthy at home and help you through  your recovery process  all the links mentioned in this video  will be in my description box below  and if you find this video to be useful  do give this video a thumbs up  share it on with your family members and  friends and let's fight together to stop  the spread of kovit 19.  do also check out other fitness videos  on my youtube channel and also a lot of  healthy recipes  and i will see you next time stay safe

